/-!
# Stacks 07SQ for bounded base changes

Let `X = lim X_i` be the limit of a directed inverse system of quasi-compact and quasi-separated
algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` with affine transition morphisms, the situation of Stacks 084R.
Stacks 07SQ — if `X` is an affine algebraic space then so is `X_i` for some `i` beyond the
distinguished index — is proved, under the chapter's convention of Section 70.2 (tag 07SD), as
`Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/DescendingProperties/AffineStage.lean`, which carries the
tag. This file records the forms of it in which the convention is replaced by an explicit size
bound on the base changes of the stages, which is what the consumers can check.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_bounded`:
  Stacks 07SQ for bounded base changes (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasBoundedBaseChanges`) at the
  stages beyond the distinguished index.
* `Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE` and
  `.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_locallyOfFiniteType`: the case of an index set below the
  cutoff whose transition morphisms enlarge affine schemes by a bounded amount, for instance closed
  immersions or finite morphisms.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_etaleCharts`: the
  case of an index set below the cutoff whose stages have surjective étale charts of uniformly
  bounded size.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasAffineStageDescent`: the case of an index set small compared to the
  cofinality of the cutoff, the statement
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasAffineStageDescentOfSmallIndex`.

## Implementation notes

*One proof.* There is a single proof of Stacks 07SQ, the one under the convention. The bounded
form is a corollary: restricting the situation to the stages at or beyond the distinguished
index (the tail `AlgebraicGeometry.LimitTail`, which is initial, so the limit is unchanged)
gives a situation all of whose stages have bounded base changes, and an inverse system with
bounded base changes at every stage satisfies the convention
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_hasBoundedBaseChanges`, through
Stacks 07SF).

*The size hypothesis.* The site is cut off at `B.cutoff`, and the limit of the charts
`U_j = X_j ×_{X_i} U` must be an object of the site for the proof to see it. That limit is affine
with ring of global functions the colimit of the `Γ(U_j)`, so it lies in the site as soon as a
single cardinal below the cutoff bounds the number of stages and every `Γ(U_j)`; this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasBoundedBaseChanges`. The bound `#I < cf(cutoff)` implies it, because
a supremum of fewer than `cf(cutoff)` cardinals below the cutoff is below the cutoff; but when the
cutoff is singular its cofinality may be as small as `ℵ₁` while the index sets of the consumers
(Stacks 07VS, 07VT) have the size of a ring of a chart, and there the bound comes instead from the
transition morphisms, which are closed immersions or finite and so do not enlarge affine schemes.

Nothing here raises a compiler limit or disables a linter.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084R)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Cardinal Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))

/-- **Stacks 07SQ for bounded base changes.** In the situation of Stacks 084R, if the limit `X`
of the inverse system is an affine algebraic space then `X_i` is an affine algebraic space for
some `i` beyond the distinguished index — provided the base changes of the stages along the
affine points of the stages are bounded below the site's size cutoff.

*The size hypothesis.* `hb i`, for each stage `i` beyond the distinguished one, says: for every
affine scheme `U` with a morphism to `X_i` there is one cardinal below the cutoff bounding the
number of stages beyond `i` and the size of every `X_j ×_{X_i} U`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasBoundedBaseChanges`). It is what keeps the limit of the affine charts
`U_j = X_j ×_{X_i} U` of the proof inside the site, so that the limit the site computes is the
limit the source speaks of. Some such hypothesis is necessary: the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Perfect/Limits.lean` describe a descent situation over a
huge index whose limit in the site is the empty algebraic space, which is affine, and none of
whose stages is affine. The hypothesis holds in the regimes the consumers meet:

* the index set is small compared to the cofinality of the cutoff
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_lt_cof`), the form of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasAffineStageDescent`;
* the index set is below the cutoff and the stages have surjective étale charts of uniformly
  bounded size
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_etaleCharts`);
* the index set is below the cutoff and the transition morphisms enlarge affine schemes by a
  bounded amount (`Space.DescentSituation.hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE`), for
  instance when their base changes to affine schemes are of finite type, as for closed immersions
  or finite morphisms
  (`Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_locallyOfFiniteType`). This needs no
  condition on the cofinality of the cutoff, which may be singular and far smaller than the index.

This is a corollary of the statement under the chapter's convention,
`Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`, which
carries the tag: the stages at or beyond the distinguished index form a situation of Stacks 084R
with the same limit, the inclusion of that tail being initial; each of its stages has bounded base
changes, the slices of the tail injecting into the slices of the index; and a system with bounded
base changes at every stage satisfies the convention
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_hasBoundedBaseChanges`). -/
theorem DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_bounded {J : Type u} [Preorder J]
    [IsDirected J (· ≤ ·)] (E : DescentSituation B S hS hZ J)
    (hb : ∀ i, E.base ≤ i → HasBoundedBaseChanges B S hS (op i) E.system)
    (hX : IsAffineSpace B S hS E.limitCone.pt) :
    ∃ j, E.base ≤ j ∧ IsAffineSpace B S hS (E.system.obj (op j)) := by
  classical
  have _ : Nonempty J := ⟨E.base⟩
  have _ : IsCofiltered Jᵒᵖ := inferInstance
  have _ : Nonempty (LimitTail J E.base) := ⟨⟨E.base, le_rfl⟩⟩
  have _ : IsDirected (LimitTail J E.base) (· ≤ ·) := by
    refine ⟨fun x y => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨k, hxk, hyk⟩ := IsDirected.directed (r := (· ≤ ·)) x.1 y.1
    exact ⟨⟨k, x.2.trans hxk⟩, hxk, hyk⟩
  have _ : IsCofiltered (LimitTail J E.base)ᵒᵖ := inferInstance
  -- the stages at or beyond the distinguished index, with the same limit
  let G : (LimitTail J E.base)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Jᵒᵖ := limitTailForget E.base
  have _ : G.Initial := by dsimp only [G, limitTailForget]; infer_instance
  let T : DescentSituation B S hS hZ (LimitTail J E.base) :=
    { system := G ⋙ E.system
      algebraicSpace := fun j => E.algebraicSpace j.1
      transition_affine := fun f => E.transition_affine (G.map f)
      quasiCompact := fun j => E.quasiCompact j.1
      quasiSeparated := fun j => E.quasiSeparated j.1
      limitCone := E.limitCone.whisker G
      isLimit := (Functor.Initial.isLimitWhiskerEquiv G E.limitCone).symm E.isLimit
      limitAlgebraicSpace := E.limitAlgebraicSpace
      base := ⟨E.base, le_rfl⟩ }
  -- every stage of the tail has bounded base changes
  have hbT : ∀ i, HasBoundedBaseChanges B S hS i T.system := by
    intro i U₀ f₀
    obtain ⟨μ, hμ, hcard, hsize⟩ := hb i.unop.1 i.unop.2 U₀ f₀
    refine ⟨μ, hμ, le_trans (Cardinal.mk_le_of_injective
      (f := fun k : Over i => (Over.post G).obj k) ?_) hcard,
      fun k W p q h => hsize ((Over.post G).obj k) W p q h⟩
    intro k₁ k₂ h
    obtain ⟨a, ⟨⟨⟩⟩, f⟩ := k₁
    obtain ⟨a', ⟨⟨⟩⟩, f'⟩ := k₂
    have ha : a = a' := Opposite.unop_injective
      (Subtype.ext (congrArg (fun k : Over (G.obj i) => k.left.unop) h))
    subst ha
    have hf : f = f' := Subsingleton.elim _ _
    subst hf
    rfl
  obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := T.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits
    (siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_hasBoundedBaseChanges T.system hbT) hX
  exact ⟨j.1, j.2, hj⟩

/-- **Stacks 07SQ for transition morphisms of bounded growth.** In the situation of Stacks 084R,
with fewer stages than the site's cutoff and every transition morphism `X_j ⟶ X_i` enlarging
affine schemes by at most a fixed `ν` below the cutoff — every `X_j ×_{X_i} T`, for `T` affine,
of size at most `max (size T) ν` — an affine limit has an affine stage. No condition on the
cofinality of the cutoff is needed. -/
theorem DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE
    {J : Type u} [Preorder J] [IsDirected J (· ≤ ·)] (E : DescentSituation B S hS hZ J)
    (hJ : #J < B.cutoff) {ν : Cardinal.{u}} (hν : ν < B.cutoff)
    (htr : ∀ {i j : Jᵒᵖ} (f : i ⟶ j), HasBaseChangesOfSizeLE B S hS ν (E.system.map f))
    (hX : IsAffineSpace B S hS E.limitCone.pt) :
    ∃ j, E.base ≤ j ∧ IsAffineSpace B S hS (E.system.obj (op j)) :=
  E.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_bounded B S hS hZ
    (fun i _ => E.hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE hJ hν htr i) hX

/-- **Stacks 07SQ for transition morphisms of finite type.** In the situation of Stacks 084R,
with fewer stages than the site's cutoff and every transition morphism locally of finite type
after base change to affine schemes — a system of closed immersions, or of finite morphisms — an
affine limit has an affine stage: such transitions do not enlarge affine schemes
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE_of_locallyOfFiniteType`). No condition on the
cofinality of the cutoff is needed. -/
theorem DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_locallyOfFiniteType
    {J : Type u} [Preorder J] [IsDirected J (· ≤ ·)] (E : DescentSituation B S hS hZ J)
    (hJ : #J < B.cutoff)
    (htr : ∀ {i j : Jᵒᵖ} (f : i ⟶ j),
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@LocallyOfFiniteType.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (E.system.map f))
    (hX : IsAffineSpace B S hS E.limitCone.pt) :
    ∃ j, E.base ≤ j ∧ IsAffineSpace B S hS (E.system.obj (op j)) :=
  E.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE B S hS hZ hJ B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
    (fun f => hasBaseChangesOfSizeLE_of_locallyOfFiniteType B S hS ℵ₀ (E.transition_affine f)
      (htr f)) hX

/-- **Stacks 07SQ for stages with uniformly bounded étale charts.** In the situation of
Stacks 084R, with fewer stages than the site's cutoff and every stage `X_j` admitting a
surjective étale chart `V_j ⟶ X_j` by an object of the site of size at most a fixed `ν` below the
cutoff, an affine limit has an affine stage. No condition on the cofinality of the cutoff is
needed: the base changes `X_j ×_{X_i} U` along an affine point are then bounded in terms of `U`
and `ν` alone (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_etaleCharts`). -/
theorem DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_etaleCharts
    {J : Type u} [Preorder J] [IsDirected J (· ≤ ·)] (E : DescentSituation B S hS hZ J)
    (hJ : #J < B.cutoff) {ν : Cardinal.{u}} (hν : ν < B.cutoff)
    (hcharts : ∀ j : J, ∃ (V : BigFppfOver B S hS) (v : yoneda.obj V ⟶ E.system.obj (op j)),
      IsEtale B S hS v ∧
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf v ∧
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V).size ≤ ν)
    (hX : IsAffineSpace B S hS E.limitCone.pt) :
    ∃ j, E.base ≤ j ∧ IsAffineSpace B S hS (E.system.obj (op j)) :=
  E.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_bounded B S hS hZ (fun i _ =>
    hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_etaleCharts B S hS (op i) E.system ((mk_over_op_le i).trans_lt hJ)
      hν fun k =>
        let ⟨V, v, he, hs, hV⟩ := hcharts k.left.unop
        ⟨V, v, (isEtale_iff_presheaf_of_yoneda B S hS v).1 he, hs, hV⟩) hX

/-- **Stacks 07SQ for an index small compared to the cofinality of the cutoff.** In the situation
of Stacks 084R, if the limit `X` of the inverse system is an affine algebraic space then `X_i` is
an affine algebraic space for some `i` beyond the distinguished index, the index set being small
compared to the cofinality of the site's size cutoff.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_bounded`:
a small index has bounded base changes
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_lt_cof`). -/
theorem hasAffineStageDescent : HasAffineStageDescentOfSmallIndex B S hS hZ := by
  intro J _ _ E hJ hX
  exact E.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_bounded B S hS hZ
    (fun i _ => E.hasBoundedBaseChanges_of_lt_cof hJ i) hX

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
